      "totalDuration": "2 yrs 9 mos",
      "description": "- Built AWS GovCloud infrastructure for several internal and customer-facing environments, including EKS, ECS, RDS, ALB, Route 53, EFS, and Bedrock.\n \n- Designed and built an EKS environment for Jira Service Management and Confluence, fully managed with Terraform, Terragrunt, and Helm, sized to scale beyond its initial use supporting service desk operations during a government fielding event.\n \n- Built a pull-based integration that fed Jira and Confluence data into Splunk during the event. It was the sole source of event reporting for leadership, covering about 100 service desk tickets with dashboards for MTTR and related metrics.\n \n- Built an ECS environment for a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) application using Bedrock, RDS, EFS, ALB, and Route 53, which was demoed several times to government leadership, including the program CTO.\n \n- Reverse-engineered the AWS architecture and data flows of five applications in a regulated environment with limited access and no existing documentation, then built a Terraform sandbox replica to prototype cross-service designs. The resulting docs became the working reference for other internal teams.\n \n- Built GitLab CI/CD and GitHub Actions pipelines to deploy Terraform-managed infrastructure and to build and deploy internal applications, with Python linting and static security scanning built in.",
