    "description": "- Worked on an internal platform team whose customers were the company's software engineers, focused on making testing and root cause analysis faster, more repeatable, and less manual.\n \n- Built Hydra, a Python test automation framework for medical devices that cut regression testing time by more than 70%. Used by five test engineers and seven software engineers, and still in use.\n \n- Built reusable Hydra modules to simulate multi-line LCD displays across several medical-device platforms, and a hardware I/O module for testing mainboards on current and next-generation products.\n \n- Built Python tooling with Pandas, NumPy, and SciPy to analyze fluorescence detection data and investigate false-positive and false-negative behavior.",
